# .rsync-exclude — transfer filter for deploy.sh
#
# WHY THIS IS AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A BLACKLIST
# ~/clawd is simultaneously the agent workspace and this repo's checkout, so
# ~860 untracked personal files (memory notes, roster CSVs, IRS PDFs, PayPal
# reports, area studies) sit beside the application. rsync does NOT read
# .gitignore, so a blacklist of names ships every new personal file that
# appears. That is exactly how MEMORY.md — with psql, Cloudflare, DigitalOcean,
# WordPress and Discord credentials in it — ended up at rest on an
# internet-facing droplet and baked into the container image layers
# (discovered 2026-09-16).
#
# So: deny by default. Only the paths named below are shipped; the final
# `- /*` rule drops every other repo-root entry. Adding a personal file to
# ~/clawd can no longer leak it.
#
# rsync applies rules in order and the FIRST match wins, which is why the
# "never ship" rules sit above the allowlist — otherwise `+ /app/***` would
# happily carry __pycache__ and *.pyc along with it.
#
# BEFORE YOU ADD A NEW TOP-LEVEL FILE THE APP NEEDS: add it here too, or it
# will not deploy. deploy.sh's post-sync REQUIRED_REMOTE_PATHS gate exists to
# catch that mistake loudly instead of silently.

# --- never ship, wherever it appears ---
- .git/
- .gitignore
- __pycache__/
- *.pyc
- *.pyo
# `.env.*` intentionally covers .env.example too — production reads .env, which
# docker-compose supplies and the --filter protect rules preserve. Nothing in
# the repo-root .env family is ever transferred, deliberately.
- .env
- .env.*
- *.bak*
- .pytest_cache/
- .ruff_cache/
- .openclaw/
- *.egg-info/

# --- the application itself ---
+ /app/***
+ /migrations/***
+ /alembic.ini
+ /config.py

# --- host-side runners invoked in production ---
# scripts/ot-instructor-notify.py runs from root's crontab (hourly guard) and
# leave_return_runner.py runs daily at 06:15, both via `docker exec` against
# /app. Dropping either silently breaks a production cron job.
#
# An allowlisted DIRECTORY still carries untracked files inside it, so scripts/
# needs per-file denies: these are local scratch, not app source, and
# nc-droplet-downsize.sh has a hardcoded DigitalOcean API token in it. The
# tracked-only leak gate in deploy.sh will abort the deploy if a new untracked
# file appears here, which is the intended loud failure — either `git add` it or
# add it below.
- /scripts/nc-droplet-downsize.sh
- /scripts/create_loadtest_event.py
- /scripts/ch-fix-dates.py
- /scripts/movie-rename.py
- /scripts/sync_ftx_and_recruit.py
+ /scripts/***
+ /leave_return_runner.py

# --- build + deploy machinery ---
+ /Dockerfile
+ /docker-compose.yml
+ /.dockerignore
+ /requirements.txt
+ /requirements-dev.txt
+ /pyproject.toml
+ /deploy.sh
+ /.rsync-exclude

# --- test suite (kept deployable so the droplet copy stays runnable) ---
+ /tests/***

+ /README.md

# --- everything else at the repo root is workspace, not application ---
- /*
